@anon.8ad231a129453d088979dfad2582f60a.1208 = private unnamed_addr constant [1324 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for function calls in default function arguments.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AAny function call that's used in a default argument will only be performed\0Aonce, at definition time. The returned value will then be reused by all\0Acalls to the function, which can lead to unexpected behaviour.\0A\0AParameters with immutable type annotations will be ignored by this rule.\0AThose whose default arguments are `NewType` calls where the original type\0Ais immutable are also ignored.\0A\0ACalls and types outside of the standard library can be marked as an exception\0Ato this rule with the [`lint.flake8-bugbear.extend-immutable-calls`] configuration option.\0A\0A## Example\0A\0A```python\0Adef create_list() -> list[int]:\0A    return [1, 2, 3]\0A\0A\0Adef mutable_default(arg: list[int] = create_list()) -> list[int]:\0A    arg.append(4)\0A    return arg\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A\0A```python\0Adef better(arg: list[int] | None = None) -> list[int]:\0A    if arg is None:\0A        arg = create_list()\0A\0A    arg.append(4)\0A    return arg\0A```\0A\0AIf the use of a singleton is intentional, assign the result call to a\0Amodule-level variable, and use that variable in the default argument:\0A\0A```python\0AERROR = ValueError(\22Hosts weren't successfully added\22)\0A\0A\0Adef add_host(error: Exception = ERROR) -> None: ...\0A```\0A\0A## Options\0A- `lint.flake8-bugbear.extend-immutable-calls`\0A", align 1
