@anon.8ad231a129453d088979dfad2582f60a.1220 = private unnamed_addr constant [1598 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for uses of mutable objects as function argument defaults.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AFunction defaults are evaluated once, when the function is defined.\0A\0AThe same mutable object is then shared across all calls to the function.\0AIf the object is modified, those modifications will persist across calls,\0Awhich can lead to unexpected behavior.\0A\0AInstead, prefer to use immutable data structures, or take `None` as a\0Adefault, and initialize a new mutable object inside the function body\0Afor each call.\0A\0AArguments with immutable type annotations will be ignored by this rule.\0ATypes outside of the standard library can be marked as immutable with the\0A[`lint.flake8-bugbear.extend-immutable-calls`] configuration option.\0A\0A## Known problems\0AMutable argument defaults can be used intentionally to cache computation\0Aresults. Replacing the default with `None` or an immutable data structure\0Adoes not work for such usages. Instead, prefer the `@functools.lru_cache`\0Adecorator from the standard library.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Adef add_to_list(item, some_list=[]):\0A    some_list.append(item)\0A    return some_list\0A\0A\0Al1 = add_to_list(0)  # [0]\0Al2 = add_to_list(1)  # [0, 1]\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Adef add_to_list(item, some_list=None):\0A    if some_list is None:\0A        some_list = []\0A    some_list.append(item)\0A    return some_list\0A\0A\0Al1 = add_to_list(0)  # [0]\0Al2 = add_to_list(1)  # [1]\0A```\0A\0A## Options\0A- `lint.flake8-bugbear.extend-immutable-calls`\0A\0A## References\0A- [Python documentation: Default Argument Values](https://docs.python.org/3/tutorial/controlflow.html#default-argument-values)\0A", align 1
