@anon.8ad231a129453d088979dfad2582f60a.1240 = private unnamed_addr constant [334 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for the unintentional use of type annotations.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AThe use of a colon (`:`) in lieu of an assignment (`=`) can be syntactically valid, but\0Ais almost certainly a mistake when used in a subscript or attribute assignment.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Aa[\22b\22]: 1\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Aa[\22b\22] = 1\0A```\0A", align 1
