@anon.8ad231a129453d088979dfad2582f60a.1269 = private unnamed_addr constant [520 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for the presence of the `from __future__ import annotations` import\0Astatement in stub files.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AStub files natively support forward references in all contexts, as stubs are\0Anever executed at runtime. (They should be thought of as \22data files\22 for\0Atype checkers.) As such, the `from __future__ import annotations` import\0Astatement has no effect and should be omitted.\0A\0A## References\0A- [Static Typing with Python: Type Stubs](https://typing.python.org/en/latest/source/stubs.html)\0A", align 1
