@anon.8ad231a129453d088979dfad2582f60a.1339 = private unnamed_addr constant [792 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for uses of `.pivot` or `.unstack` on Pandas objects.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0APrefer `.pivot_table` to `.pivot` or `.unstack`. `.pivot_table` is more general\0Aand can be used to implement the same behavior as `.pivot` and `.unstack`.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Aimport pandas as pd\0A\0Adf = pd.read_csv(\22cities.csv\22)\0Adf.pivot(index=\22city\22, columns=\22year\22, values=\22population\22)\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Aimport pandas as pd\0A\0Adf = pd.read_csv(\22cities.csv\22)\0Adf.pivot_table(index=\22city\22, columns=\22year\22, values=\22population\22)\0A```\0A\0A## References\0A- [Pandas documentation: Reshaping and pivot tables](https://pandas.pydata.org/docs/user_guide/reshaping.html)\0A- [Pandas documentation: `pivot_table`](https://pandas.pydata.org/docs/reference/api/pandas.pivot_table.html#pandas.pivot_table)\0A", align 1
