@anon.8ad231a129453d088979dfad2582f60a.1357 = private unnamed_addr constant [1507 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for undocumented public module definitions.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0APublic modules should be documented via docstrings to outline their purpose\0Aand contents.\0A\0AGenerally, module docstrings should describe the purpose of the module and\0Alist the classes, exceptions, functions, and other objects that are exported\0Aby the module, alongside a one-line summary of each.\0A\0AIf the module is a script, the docstring should be usable as its \22usage\22\0Amessage.\0A\0AIf the codebase adheres to a standard format for module docstrings, follow\0Athat format for consistency.\0A\0A## Example\0A\0A```python\0Aclass FasterThanLightError(ZeroDivisionError): ...\0A\0A\0Adef calculate_speed(distance: float, time: float) -> float: ...\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A\0A```python\0A\22\22\22Utility functions and classes for calculating speed.\0A\0AThis module provides:\0A- FasterThanLightError: exception when FTL speed is calculated;\0A- calculate_speed: calculate speed given distance and time.\0A\22\22\22\0A\0A\0Aclass FasterThanLightError(ZeroDivisionError): ...\0A\0A\0Adef calculate_speed(distance: float, time: float) -> float: ...\0A```\0A\0A## Notebook behavior\0AThis rule is ignored for Jupyter Notebooks.\0A\0A## References\0A- [PEP 257 \E2\80\93 Docstring Conventions](https://peps.python.org/pep-0257/)\0A- [PEP 287 \E2\80\93 reStructuredText Docstring Format](https://peps.python.org/pep-0287/)\0A- [NumPy Style Guide](https://numpydoc.readthedocs.io/en/latest/format.html)\0A- [Google Python Style Guide - Docstrings](https://google.github.io/styleguide/pyguide.html#38-comments-and-docstrings)\0A", align 1
